# AUDIT_REQUEST — round r001, Phase: S1 novelty, closest-three lock (2026-09-16)

## Roles and scope
Builder = Claude Code; Auditor = Codex (assignment: research/STATE.yaml, PI-confirmed 2026-09-16). This request is the BLIND phase of the S1 novelty protocol: neutral task-space description + raw corpus only. It contains no builder pitch, no claimed contributions, no expected answers. Budget: single non-interactive run, no network required (corpus provided; your own knowledge allowed if flagged). Write ONLY under out/.

## Task space (neutral description)
A planned research project will evaluate the safety of conversational AI (LLMs) for adolescent users (ages 12–17) in the Korean language and cultural context, with multi-turn conversations. Risk areas under consideration include: grooming/sexual exploitation, boundary violation/manipulation, identity confusion/anthropomorphism, emotional overdependence/isolation, self-harm/suicide/crisis response, and companion-app-specific risks. The evaluation is also concerned with helpfulness and over-refusal on benign inputs, and with how model responses are scored (human raters and/or LLM judges).

## Instructions to the Auditor
1. Read CORPUS.md in this directory (A: verified works; B: deduplicated arXiv query hits from a dated sweep executed 2026-09-16).
2. Select and LOCK the THREE existing works closest to the task space above — closest overall, considering population (minors/adolescents), interaction structure (multi-turn/longitudinal), risk constructs (relational/emotional/crisis), language/cultural scope, and evaluation methodology. You may name a work not in the corpus from your own knowledge; mark it [OWN-KNOWLEDGE] and give your best identifier (title + venue/year); do not fabricate identifiers.
3. Write out/CLOSEST_THREE.md with: (a) a LOCK header line: date, tool, model, the sentence "Locked before seeing any builder pitch."; (b) the three locked works, each with id/title/date and 2–4 sentences on why it is closest; (c) up to five runners-up with one line each; (d) one paragraph: what any new project in this space must differentiate itself from, judging ONLY from the corpus and your knowledge — do not speculate about what the builder intends.
4. Do not read any other file in the repository. Do not modify anything outside out/.
