+AUDIT_REPORT — r001 / S1 informed novelty assessment / 2026-09-16
+
+Actual auditor: **Codex; model: GPT-6**, as identified in this session. No separate reviewer or sub-agent was used. The existing Phase-A lock was retained; this report was written after reading the builder pitch.
+
+The supplied evidence does **not establish that a locked work already delivers the complete proposed core**. It also does **not establish that the core is new**. The builder repeatedly treats missing information in short excerpts as demonstrated absence in prior work. The defensible present classification is a **proposed benchmark extension with domain-specific integration of measurement methods**, plus a potentially substantive measurement hypothesis whose novelty and importance remain unresolved. Recommendation: **AWAITING_PI**; no outcome-changing anticipation of the complete core is demonstrated by this corpus.
+
+The request was located in `/home/wjeong/adol/audit/r001`, rather than the workspace root. All references below concern that audit package. Substantive inputs read:
+
+- [PHASE_B_REQUEST.md](/home/wjeong/adol/audit/r001/PHASE_B_REQUEST.md), complete: current instructions and output contract.
+- [AUDIT_REQUEST.md](/home/wjeong/adol/audit/r001/AUDIT_REQUEST.md), complete: Phase-A scope and provenance; its blind-phase access restriction was not reapplied to the explicitly informed phase.
+- [out/CLOSEST_THREE.md](/home/wjeong/adol/audit/r001/out/CLOSEST_THREE.md), complete: the fixed three works, five runners-up, and differentiation paragraph. No selection was changed.
+- [CORPUS.md](/home/wjeong/adol/audit/r001/CORPUS.md), all 162 lines, both sections. Citation shorthand **C:line** identifies an entry in this file.
+- [NOVELTY_MATRIX.md](/home/wjeong/adol/audit/r001/NOVELTY_MATRIX.md), all 30 lines. Citation shorthand **M:line**.
+- [REJECT_MEMO.md](/home/wjeong/adol/audit/r001/REJECT_MEMO.md), all 30 lines. Citation shorthand **R:line**.
+
+Filesystem listings, working-tree status, and incidental discovery matches in existing run logs were not used as novelty evidence. No external sources or own-knowledge literature additions were used.
+
+C:2 defines the evidence as identifiers, dates, titles, and abstract heads. “Verified” in this package concerns the supplied metadata; it does not establish the detailed methods or exclusions in the builder's rows. Below, **unestablished** means the excerpt is insufficient, not that the feature is absent. Builder-only assertions are identified as such rather than independently confirmed.
